	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["21FBC75CF8ACF1C4"]
			description: ["The most-used subcomponent, you'll need a lot of these. You should start by going for the Tool Replacement machines, as they typically offer more efficient recipes which will make further machines easier."]
			id: "7185027130B5CEB3"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4C39243963F81ADD"
				item: "gtceu:lv_electric_motor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Subcomponent 1"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7185027130B5CEB3"]
			description: [
				"Despite not being used in many recipes, the Pump is still vital for you to make several of, as it has another use:"
				""
				"You can place it against a block with a pipe connected, and then shift right-click the cover placed to configure it. Once placed, the pump will insert or extract fluids from the connected block into the pipe network as configured."
				""
				"One thing to note is that the 'insert' mode inserts &lto the pipe network&r, whereas 'extract' inserts to the block."
			]
			id: "0CF46145C49B1D0A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2FE41375D4A7DB10"
				item: "gtceu:lv_electric_pump"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Subcomponent 2"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7185027130B5CEB3"]
			description: ["While not used in as many things, mechanical pistons are still used for some important machine and so you'll need several of them."]
			id: "241CE7D5D474CF73"
			tasks: [{
				id: "26468CA4F32BF1DF"
				item: "gtceu:lv_electric_piston"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Subcomponent 3"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0FE7D58658BF9803"]
			description: [
				"The way GregTech's power system works is based on a series of voltage tiers. "
				"Starting from LV and going up to OpV, these tiers each represent how much EU is contained within 1 Amp of current. LV has 32 EU/Amp, with each subsequent voltage tier multiplying this value by 4."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Machines and cables are each rated for a specific voltage tier and amperage. "
				"Attempting to run more current through a wire than it can handle will set it on fire, whereas a machine provided with a higher voltage than it can deal with will explode."
				"Machines will take only the amps specified by the recipe they are running, or 1 amp when their energy buffer isn't full, which means you can use a multi-amp cable to power several machines. "
				"This also means you should use a cable that is the same voltage tier as the machine it powers, as using a lower tier cable would result in the machine not being able to draw enough power."
			]
			id: "21FBC75CF8ACF1C4"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5F298FB67011EBB5"
				title: "Understanding Voltage"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7185027130B5CEB3"]
			description: ["Like the Electric Pump, the Conveyer can be placed on a block connected to Item Pipes, functioning the same way."]
			id: "2FA18A0CDDBB4796"
			tasks: [{
				id: "271394673D930A27"
				item: "gtceu:lv_conveyor_module"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Subcomponent 4"
			x: 3.5d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"7185027130B5CEB3"
				"241CE7D5D474CF73"
			]
			description: ["The Robot Arm can be placed just like a Conveyer, functioning the exact same except for the addition of an option to limit the number of items transferred when the network or block has a specific number of the items it transfers."]
			id: "78BED48F1B7AD244"
